implementationPlan.description:
THE COMMAND EDGE THAT WRITES THE RETIREMENT FACT.

New `apps/daemon/src/monitoring/environment-retirement-command-contracts.ts` and `environment-retirement-command.ts`, modelled on the `probe-interval-command*.ts` pair beside them — read both first. The contracts module owns the payload's fixed shape and its FIXED refusal codes; the command module serves the kind and writes child 1's fact.

WIRE IT in `apps/daemon/src/daemon-command-registry.ts` following :60-61 (imports), :232 (construct the record ONCE), :547-556 (dispatch). READ THE COMMENT AT :547 — "THE ONE PORT, SHARED" — and honour it: the retirement record must be constructed ONCE and be the SAME instance the sweep's predicate reads. Two instances over one store means a retirement is durable but invisible until restart, and both this row's arms and child 2's would pass while the feature does not work. This is the single most likely way this row ships broken.

EVERY REFUSAL CARRIES A STABLE CODE ASSERTED WITH ITS LAYER. Two layers can answer here — the operator fence, and child 1's own name/unknown-environment refusals — so every arm pins WHICH one refused. A test asserting only "it refused" is one added layer away from vacuous (project rail 1).

ARMS, in a new `environment-retirement-command.test.ts`:
(a) an operator retires an environment and the child-1 fact is written;
(b) a NON-operator principal is refused, asserting the code AND the fence's layer;
(c) an invalid or unknown environment name is refused, asserting the code AND that the RECORD's layer answered, not the fence's;
(d) RETIREMENT IS NOT DESTRUCTION: after success, the environment's deploy receipts still read back through `readDeployLedger` and its probe ring is still readable. Assert CONTENT, not merely that a call returned — a reader that silently answers empty passes a shallow check.
(e) END TO END, the proof the parent row ultimately wants: dispatch the command, then run a sweep tick, and assert NO new sample was recorded for the retired name. Child 2 landed the reader; this arm proves the writer reaches it through the shared instance.
